                      (    forth6809.asm):05209                                  ; testing CLR's result, not n1's actual sign.
                      (    forth6809.asm):05210                                  ; BPL always branched, meaning n1 was NEVER
                      (    forth6809.asm):05211                                  ; negated even when genuinely negative - found
                      (    forth6809.asm):05212                                  ; via MAME: TSTMSTAR's two returned values
                      (    forth6809.asm):05213                                  ; came back wrong, which turned out to be
                      (    forth6809.asm):05214                                  ; this, not a push-order swap in the test
                      (    forth6809.asm):05215                                  ; itself. FMSLASHMOD/SMSLASHREM already do
                      (    forth6809.asm):05216                                  ; this correctly (explicit TST PRODHI between
                      (    forth6809.asm):05217                                  ; their own CLR calls and the branch) - MSTAR
                      (    forth6809.asm):05218                                  ; was simply missing the equivalent re-test.
